# Bentley S1 four-door standard saloon, 1955-1959.
#
# The S1 was the Bentley version of the Rolls-Royce Silver Cloud I: 5,384 mm
# long, 1,829 mm wide, 1,600 mm high, 3,124 mm wheelbase; 4,887 cc six,
# automatic transmission, and the last of the separate-chassis Bentleys.
# 3,072 S1 standards built, plus 145 long-wheelbase and 431 Continentals.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bentley_S_series
#
# Colours: Black, Shell Grey, Maroon and Sage Green were period Bentley
# finishes.
#
# Weight: 12 in total (black 5, silver 3, maroon 2, grey 2). Section F: the
# 1940s-50s class-4 row needs a British representative and the S1 is it.
#
# Speed 165 km/h; comfort 85/458 (line). Classes 3,4.
# Dates: 1955-1959 with a road tail to about 1980.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/bentley-s1.blend. References:
# citycars/references/bentley-s1/ (gitignored). Images via Wikimedia Commons.

obj=citycar
